{"id":"288977f8607c0661","group":"17","path":"17/17-thm-elementary-chain-union.md","title":"Union of an Elementary Chain","display":"thm-elementary-chain-union — Union of an Elementary Chain","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Model Theory (Chang & Keisler, 3rd ed. 1990)","book_abbrev":"17","label":"17-thm-elementary-chain-union","aliases":["17-thm-elementary-chain-union"],"display":"thm-elementary-chain-union — Union of an Elementary Chain","depends_on":["[[17-df-elementary-chain]]","[[17-df-structure]]","[[17-df-elementary-substructure]]","[[17-df-chain-union]]"],"source_section":"3.1","source_result":"Theorem 3.1.9 (Elementary Chain Theorem)","source_pages_print":[140,141],"source_pages_djvu":[156,157],"source_verification":"statement and induction proof compared in supplied OCR; local nonempty linear-index generalization","label_origin":"local-catalog","legacy_label":"17-thm-3.1.2","local_revision":"content audit of supplied 17(1).zip; inherited source_verification and bibliographic fields not independently reverified"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Model Theory (Chang &amp; Keisler, 3rd ed. 1990)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"17"},{"key":"label","html":"17-thm-elementary-chain-union"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>17-thm-elementary-chain-union</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-elementary-chain-union — Union of an Elementary Chain"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"9a564fd35615a768\" href=\"?note=9a564fd35615a768\" title=\"17-df-elementary-chain\">17-df-elementary-chain</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"fdac06af5a7f3bb5\" href=\"?note=fdac06af5a7f3bb5\" title=\"17-df-structure\">17-df-structure</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"71ede582cb78a069\" href=\"?note=71ede582cb78a069\" title=\"17-df-elementary-substructure\">17-df-elementary-substructure</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"cbea1b33aeed1412\" href=\"?note=cbea1b33aeed1412\" title=\"17-df-chain-union\">17-df-chain-union</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_section","html":"3.1"},{"key":"source_result","html":"Theorem 3.1.9 (Elementary Chain Theorem)"},{"key":"source_pages_print","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>140</span><span>141</span></div>"},{"key":"source_pages_djvu","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>156</span><span>157</span></div>"},{"key":"source_verification","html":"statement and induction proof compared in supplied OCR; local nonempty linear-index generalization"},{"key":"label_origin","html":"local-catalog"},{"key":"legacy_label","html":"17-thm-3.1.2"},{"key":"local_revision","html":"content audit of supplied 17(1).zip; inherited source_verification and bibliographic fields not independently reverified"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\\in\\mathrm{FirstOrderLanguages}\">\\(L\\in\\mathrm{FirstOrderLanguages}\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"I\\neq\\varnothing\">\\(I\\neq\\varnothing\\)</span> 且 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{StrictLinearOrder}(I,&lt;)\">\\(\\operatorname{StrictLinearOrder}(I,&lt;)\\)</span>；严格序谓词采用 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"9a564fd35615a768\" href=\"?note=9a564fd35615a768\" title=\"17-df-elementary-chain\">17-df-elementary-chain</a> 的本册依赖。</p>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(I,&lt;)\">\\((I,&lt;)\\)</span> is a nonempty linear order and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(\\mathfrak A_i)_{i\\in I}\">\\((\\mathfrak A_i)_{i\\in I}\\)</span> is a family of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\">\\(L\\)</span>-structures.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{ElemChain}_L\">\\(\\operatorname{ElemChain}_L\\)</span> is from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"9a564fd35615a768\" href=\"?note=9a564fd35615a768\" title=\"17-df-elementary-chain\">17-df-elementary-chain</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{ChainUnion}_L\">\\(\\operatorname{ChainUnion}_L\\)</span> is from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"cbea1b33aeed1412\" href=\"?note=cbea1b33aeed1412\" title=\"17-df-chain-union\">17-df-chain-union</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\preceq_L\">\\(\\preceq_L\\)</span> is from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"71ede582cb78a069\" href=\"?note=71ede582cb78a069\" title=\"17-df-elementary-substructure\">17-df-elementary-substructure</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\operatorname{ElemChain}_L(I,&lt;,(\\mathfrak A_i)_{i\\in I})\n\\to{}&amp;\\exists\\mathfrak B\\in\\mathrm{Structure}(L)\\;\n\\operatorname{ChainUnion}_L(I,&lt;,(\\mathfrak A_i)_{i\\in I},\\mathfrak B)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall\\mathfrak B\\in\\mathrm{Structure}(L)\\;\n\\Bigl(\\operatorname{ChainUnion}_L(I,&lt;,(\\mathfrak A_i)_{i\\in I},\\mathfrak B)\n\\to\\forall i\\in I\\;(\\mathfrak A_i\\preceq_L\\mathfrak B)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\operatorname{ElemChain}_L(I,&lt;,(\\mathfrak A_i)_{i\\in I})\n\\to{}&amp;\\exists\\mathfrak B\\in\\mathrm{Structure}(L)\\;\n\\operatorname{ChainUnion}_L(I,&lt;,(\\mathfrak A_i)_{i\\in I},\\mathfrak B)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall\\mathfrak B\\in\\mathrm{Structure}(L)\\;\n\\Bigl(\\operatorname{ChainUnion}_L(I,&lt;,(\\mathfrak A_i)_{i\\in I},\\mathfrak B)\n\\to\\forall i\\in I\\;(\\mathfrak A_i\\preceq_L\\mathfrak B)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>This is the Elementary Chain Theorem 3.1.9, printed pp. 140–141, DjVu pages 156–157, expressed using the explicit union predicate. The book uses ordinal indices. The proof by induction on formulas works for any nonempty linear index order: finitely many parameters and one existential witness occur together at a stage. Lemma 3.1.8 supplies existence of the union structure. This local label differs from the original theorem number.</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"17-df-elementary-chain","status":"resolved","id":"9a564fd35615a768","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[17-df-elementary-chain]]","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-structure","status":"resolved","id":"fdac06af5a7f3bb5","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[17-df-structure]]","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-elementary-substructure","status":"resolved","id":"71ede582cb78a069","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[17-df-elementary-substructure]]","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-chain-union","status":"resolved","id":"cbea1b33aeed1412","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[17-df-chain-union]]","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-elementary-chain","status":"resolved","id":"9a564fd35615a768","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$L\\in\\mathrm{FirstOrderLanguages}$，$I\\neq\\varnothing$ 且 $\\operatorname{StrictLinearOrder}(I,<)$；严格序谓词采用 [[17-df-elementary-chain]] 的本册依赖。","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-elementary-chain","status":"resolved","id":"9a564fd35615a768","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{ElemChain}_L$ is from [[17-df-elementary-chain]].","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-chain-union","status":"resolved","id":"cbea1b33aeed1412","anchor":"ref-7","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{ChainUnion}_L$ is from [[17-df-chain-union]].","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-elementary-substructure","status":"resolved","id":"71ede582cb78a069","anchor":"ref-8","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\preceq_L$ is from [[17-df-elementary-substructure]].","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"L\\in\\mathrm{FirstOrderLanguages}","display":false},{"tex":"I\\neq\\varnothing","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{StrictLinearOrder}(I,<)","display":false},{"tex":"(I,<)","display":false},{"tex":"(\\mathfrak A_i)_{i\\in I}","display":false},{"tex":"L","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{ElemChain}_L","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{ChainUnion}_L","display":false},{"tex":"\\preceq_L","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\operatorname{ElemChain}_L(I,<,(\\mathfrak A_i)_{i\\in I})\n\\to{}&\\exists\\mathfrak B\\in\\mathrm{Structure}(L)\\;\n\\operatorname{ChainUnion}_L(I,<,(\\mathfrak A_i)_{i\\in I},\\mathfrak B)\\\\\n&\\land\\forall\\mathfrak B\\in\\mathrm{Structure}(L)\\;\n\\Bigl(\\operatorname{ChainUnion}_L(I,<,(\\mathfrak A_i)_{i\\in I},\\mathfrak B)\n\\to\\forall i\\in I\\;(\\mathfrak A_i\\preceq_L\\mathfrak B)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true}],"bytes":2233,"backlinks":[{"id":"4646e8fdeb7322ed","anchor":"ref-5","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"256a095d7318cb9c","anchor":"ref-8","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$L$ 固定，$T,T^*,T^{**}\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_L$。\n$\\operatorname{ModelCompanion}_L$ 见 [[17-df-model-companion]]，$\\operatorname{Mod}$ 见 [[17-df-model]]。\n证明使用 [[17-lem-universal-consequences-extension]] 的延拓及 [[17-thm-elementary-chain-union]] 的初等链定理。"},{"id":"2c98c9e634ff4b44","anchor":"ref-175","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[17-thm-aleph-one-categoricity-consequences]]\n[[17-thm-atomic-model-existence]]\n[[17-thm-beth-definability]]\n[[